//@version=6
strategy("SPX ORB 3-Bot v1 STRATEGY — Bot1 orders + spread alerts", shorttitle="SPX-ORB 3BOT S", overlay=true,
     initial_capital=20000, default_qty_type=strategy.fixed, default_qty_value=10,
     margin_long=33.333, margin_short=33.333,
     calc_on_every_tick=false, process_orders_on_close=true, max_labels_count=500)

// STATUS 2026-08-17 (v1.2.2): STRATEGY companion to pine/SPX_ORB_3BOT_v1.pine (same signals) —
// v1.2.2 (2026-08-17): ACCOUNT DEFAULTS ONLY, no signal logic touched. initial_capital
//   10,000 -> 20,000; default_qty_value 1 -> 10; "Option contracts" 1 -> 10; margin 33.333%
//   (= 3x leverage). Set on user instruction. READ THE THREE WARNINGS BELOW BEFORE TRADING IT.
// v1.2.1 (2026-08-08): BOT1 entries blocked on the session's FINAL bar (15:55) — see the
//   `rthIx < 77` note at the signal block. No other change.
//
// *** WARNING 1 — 10 CONTRACTS IS NOT SURVIVABLE ON $20,000 AT THE DOCUMENTED WORST DAYS. ***
// Every backtest figure in this file is PER CONTRACT. Multiplied by 10 against a $20,000 account:
//     BOT1 worst day       -$6,980/ct  ->  -$69,800   = 349% of the account
//     BOT1+BOT3L worst day -$2,680/ct  ->  -$26,800   = 134% of the account
//     BOT3L worst day      -$2,150/ct  ->  -$21,500   = 108% of the account
// The live forward window (2026-07-17..08-14) already shows a -$1,515/ct day = -$15,150 at 10ct,
// i.e. 76% of the account in one session. Premium at 10ct commits $8,000-$30,600 per BOT1 entry;
// the top of that range EXCEEDS the account outright, and holding BOT1+BOT3L together needs
// ~$21,500 at 10ct against $20,000 of capital. Sizing is the user's call, but the arithmetic is
// not in dispute: at 10 fixed contracts this account is a total-loss candidate on a single
// documented-magnitude day.
//
// *** WARNING 2 — "3x LEVERAGE" DOES NOT EXIST FOR THIS STRATEGY AT A BROKER. ***
// The margin_long/margin_short=33.333 above only changes TradingView's Strategy Tester. Under
// Reg T a LONG option position is 100% CASH — it is not marginable at any leverage, and 0DTE
// least of all. The broker will reject anything the cash balance cannot pay for outright. Treat
// the buying power available to this system as $20,000, not $60,000.
//
// *** WARNING 3 — FIXED CONTRACTS DISCARDS THE LARGEST SINGLE SOURCE OF EDGE. ***
// A flat contract count cannot skip rich-premium days, and the rich tercile is NET NEGATIVE
// (-$61,310, PF 0.77) and hosts the worst day. Fixed-DOLLAR risk sizing returned +$452,985 over
// 4.5yr vs +$205,025 at flat 1ct, with a 4.3x smaller worst day. Risk/ct = HALF the premium, so
// on a $20,000 account a 10%-per-day budget = $2,000 risk = ~3 contracts at the median $1,220
// premium and ~5 at the cheap end — it only reaches 10 contracts on genuinely cheap days, which
// is the point. To get that behaviour set "Option quantity mode" = "TradersPost sizing" and put
// $4,000 in TradersPost's "Amount per position" (verify in paper FIRST — see that tooltip).
//
//
// *** SECOND AUTOMATED LEG ADDED 2026-08-07: pine/SPX_ORB_BOT3L_60M_v1_strategy.pine ***
// BOT3's 60m OR now trades as a SINGLE-LEG long ATM option (the 10-wide spread was never
// automatable — the TradersPost payload is single-leg only). RUN IT AS A SEPARATE STRATEGY ON
// ITS OWN CHART WITH ITS OWN ALERT. Do NOT merge it into this file: TradingView nets positions
// within a strategy, and BOT1/BOT3 break in OPPOSITE directions on 25% of days, so a merged
// BOT3 entry would net against an open BOT1 position and silently flatten it.
//
// *** WARNING — THE FIXED $2,000 PREMIUM SKIP BELOW IS DRIFTING (found 2026-08-07). ***
// It is a fixed DOLLAR threshold on a premium that scales with the index, so it tightens as SPX
// rises: $2,000 was 0.49% of spot in 2022 but only 0.28% in 2026. Per-year on BOT1:
//   no skip      : 2022 +58,425  2023 +63,415  2024 +14,775  2025 +40,945  2026 +27,755
//   skip > $2,000: 2022 +113,015 2023 +124,595 2024 +22,525  2025  +6,425  2026  +3,965
// It nearly doubles the early years and GUTS the recent ones — the headline +$452,985 is NOT a
// go-forward expectation. A relative cap (0.45% of spot) recovers part of it but only beat
// no-skip in 2/4 live years on BOT1, which is not clean enough to adopt off a sweep. THIS FILE IS
// THEREFORE UNCHANGED pending forward evidence; if you use TradersPost sizing, revisit "Amount
// per position" as SPX moves rather than leaving it fixed. (The identical test on BOT3-LONG came
// back clean at 3/4 live years, which is why the new leg ships with a relative cap.)
//
// SEPARATE from the UDB-ORB TSLA suite. Chart: SPX, 5-minute, RTH.
// v1.1 CHANGES (no signal logic touched): header synced to the 2026-07-24 re-verification;
//   NEW "Option quantity mode" input (default = unchanged) wiring the fixed-DOLLAR sizing that
//   was validated on 2026-07-24 but never reached this file; exit JSON no longer hardcodes a
//   quantity (action=exit closes the whole position — required for sizing mode, and safer in
//   both modes since the strategy cannot know a broker-sized contract count).
// WHAT THIS AUTOMATES (via TradersPost webhook, Order asset = Options):
//   BOT1 15m OR break -> BUY ATM 0DTE (CALL up / PUT dn), and CLOSE at the 30-min TIME STOP
//   (or EOD failsafe). The +50%/-50% PREMIUM brackets are NOT chart-executable (the chart
//   cannot see option prices) — place them as a broker-side OCO after the fill, or manage
//   manually. The time stop + EOD exits ARE automated here.
//   BOT2/BOT3 credit spreads = ALERTS ONLY (multi-leg orders are not webhook-able here);
//   use the alertcondition()s and place the spread at the broker.
// Strategy Tester shows INDEX-POINT P&L of the Bot1 timing only (a proxy) — real option P&L
// (premium, theta, IV) is NOT backtestable in TV. The REAL numbers are the OPRA backtest,
// BARCLOSE-CORRECTED 2026-07-24 (the originals had a 5-min entry lookahead — bar-START quotes):
// FULL 2022-2026 @1ct: BOT1 ts30 +$205,025 (was +$457,265; WR 48%, PF 1.50, worst -$6,980),
// COMBO +$687,671 (was +$1,088,751). Every bot positive every year; see docs/SPX_ANALYSIS.md.
// SIZING (re-verified 2026-07-24): the RICH premium tercile is NET NEGATIVE (-$61,310, PF 0.77)
// and hosts the -$6,980 worst day. Capping BOT1 risk at $1k/day — risk/ct = HALF the premium,
// so skip when premium > ~$2,000 — returns +$452,985 / 4.5yr (2.2x the flat-1ct +$205,025) with
// the worst day cut to -$1,610 (4.3x smaller), trading 726 of 1107 days. Most of that gain is
// the SKIP of rich days, not the contract count. See "Option quantity mode" below.
// Forward ledger: forward_test_spx.py (daily, T+1; barclose-corrected + rebuilt same day).

// ==================== INPUTS ====================
bufPct     = input.float(0.05, "Break buffer (% of OR level)", minval=0.0, step=0.01, group="Signal") * 0.01
tsMin      = input.int(30, "Bot1 time stop (minutes)", minval=5, step=5, group="Bot1")
optQtyMode = input.string("Fixed contracts", "Option quantity mode", options=["Fixed contracts", "TradersPost sizing (omit quantity)"], group="Bot1 · TradersPost", tooltip="Fixed contracts (default) = the webhook sends the 'Option contracts' quantity below, i.e. v1.0 behaviour, unchanged. 'TradersPost sizing' = the entry JSON OMITS the quantity field so TradersPost's strategy-level position sizing decides the contract count — set 'Amount per position' to ~$2,000 there (= the $1k/day risk cap, since risk/ct is HALF the premium). WHY: the 2026-07-24 re-verification found the RICH premium tercile is net NEGATIVE (-$61,310, PF 0.77) and hosts the -$6,980 worst day; a $1k risk cap auto-skips those days for +$452,985 / 4.5yr vs +$205,025 flat-1ct, worst day -$1,610. VERIFY IN PAPER FIRST — two things TradersPost's docs do not settle: (1) whether 'Amount per position' divides by the option PREMIUM (correct) or the INDEX price (very wrong — SPX ~6,000 would size 0 contracts every day), and (2) whether an unaffordable day SKIPS or errors. The skip is where most of the edge lives, so confirm it on a real fill before trusting it.")
optContracts = input.int(10, "Option contracts (quantity)", minval=1, group="Bot1 · TradersPost", tooltip="Used only in 'Fixed contracts' mode. Default raised 1 -> 10 on 2026-08-17 by user instruction. THIS IS THE ONLY SIZING FIELD THAT REACHES THE BROKER — initial_capital and default_qty_value affect the Strategy Tester display only, because the chart trades the INDEX, not the option. All backtest figures are PER CONTRACT: at 10ct the documented BOT1 worst day is -$69,800 against a $20,000 account (349%), and premium commits $8,000-$30,600 per entry. Median SPX premium ~$1,220/ct (p90 ~$5,400); risk/ct = half premium. See WARNING 1 and WARNING 3 in the header — flat contracts cannot skip the net-negative rich-premium tercile, which is where most of the edge lives.")
optQtyFixed  = str.startswith(optQtyMode, "Fixed")
otmPct     = input.float(0.30, "Spread short leg OTM %", step=0.05, group="Bots 2/3 (alerts only)") * 0.01
strikeStep = input.float(5.0, "Strike spacing", group="Bots 2/3 (alerts only)")
enB2       = input.bool(true, "Bot2 30m spread alerts", group="Bots 2/3 (alerts only)")
enB3       = input.bool(true, "Bot3 60m spread alerts", group="Bots 2/3 (alerts only)")

isRTH  = not na(time(timeframe.period, "0930-1600", "America/New_York"))
newDay = ta.change(time("D")) != 0
if barstate.isfirst and not (timeframe.isintraday and timeframe.multiplier == 5)
    runtime.error("SPX-ORB 3BOT requires a 5-minute chart.")
var int rthIx = na
rthIx := isRTH ? (na(rthIx[1]) or newDay ? 0 : nz(rthIx[1]) + 1) : na

// ==================== OR TRACKING ====================
var float hi15 = na, var float lo15 = na
var float hi30 = na, var float lo30 = na
var float hi60 = na, var float lo60 = na
if isRTH and rthIx == 0
    hi15 := high, lo15 := low
    hi30 := high, lo30 := low
    hi60 := high, lo60 := low
if isRTH and rthIx > 0
    if rthIx <= 2
        hi15 := math.max(hi15, high), lo15 := math.min(lo15, low)
    if rthIx <= 5
        hi30 := math.max(hi30, high), lo30 := math.min(lo30, low)
    if rthIx <= 11
        hi60 := math.max(hi60, high), lo60 := math.min(lo60, low)

// ==================== SIGNALS ====================
var int b1Dir = 0, var int b2Dir = 0, var int b3Dir = 0
var int b1Bar = na
if newDay
    b1Dir := 0, b2Dir := 0, b3Dir := 0, b1Bar := na
// v1.2.1: `rthIx < 77` blocks an entry on the FINAL bar of the session (15:55) — that entry can
// never be closed (the EOD failsafe skips the entry bar because position_size is still 0, there is
// no later RTH bar, and `newDay` nulls b1Bar so the time stop dies too), so it would carry to the
// next session while the 0DTE option expires. Same guard as SPX_ORB_BOT3L_60M_v1_strategy.pine.
b1Up = isRTH and rthIx > 2  and rthIx < 77 and b1Dir == 0 and close > hi15 * (1 + bufPct)
b1Dn = isRTH and rthIx > 2  and rthIx < 77 and b1Dir == 0 and close < lo15 * (1 - bufPct)
b2Up = enB2 and isRTH and rthIx > 5  and b2Dir == 0 and close > hi30 * (1 + bufPct)
b2Dn = enB2 and isRTH and rthIx > 5  and b2Dir == 0 and close < lo30 * (1 - bufPct)
b3Up = enB3 and isRTH and rthIx > 11 and b3Dir == 0 and close > hi60 * (1 + bufPct)
b3Dn = enB3 and isRTH and rthIx > 11 and b3Dir == 0 and close < lo60 * (1 - bufPct)

// ==================== BOT1 ORDERS (TradersPost options webhook) ====================
// TradingView alert message must be {{strategy.order.alert_message}} (same as the TSLA v3 setup).
// TradersPost: entries are always action=buy with optionType carrying direction (buy CALL up / buy PUT dn).
// Leave the opt-in "Invert puts" strategy setting UNCHECKED — with an explicit put contract in the signal,
// invert-ON would flip action=buy into SELL-TO-OPEN a short put.
// "+0 days" is safe to hardcode HERE because SPX lists an expiry EVERY trading day (true 0DTE daily);
// TSLA does NOT (~Mon/Wed/Fri only) — that's why the TSLA v3 strategy needs its expiration dropdown.
// v1.1: in "TradersPost sizing" mode the quantity field is OMITTED so TradersPost's own
// position sizing ("Amount per position") sets the contract count — an explicit quantity in
// the JSON would override it. Fixed mode is byte-identical to v1.0.
f_optMsg(action, cp) =>
    qpart = optQtyFixed ? '"quantity":' + str.tostring(optContracts) + ', ' : ''
    '{"ticker":"SPX", "action":"' + action + '", ' + qpart + '"expiration":"+0 days", "optionType":"' + cp + '", "strikesAway":0}'
if b1Up or b1Dn
    b1Dir := b1Up ? 1 : -1
    b1Bar := bar_index
    if b1Up
        strategy.entry("B1", strategy.long, alert_message=f_optMsg("buy", "call"))
    else
        strategy.entry("B1", strategy.short, alert_message=f_optMsg("buy", "put"))
tsBars = math.max(1, math.round(tsMin / 5.0))
b1TimeStop = strategy.position_size != 0 and not na(b1Bar) and bar_index >= b1Bar + tsBars
b1EOD      = strategy.position_size != 0 and isRTH and rthIx >= 76      // 15:50 bar onward
if b1TimeStop or b1EOD
    // v1.1: no quantity on the exit — action=exit closes the WHOLE position. Required in
    // TradersPost-sizing mode (the strategy cannot know the broker-chosen contract count) and
    // safer in fixed mode too, where a stale quantity would leave a partial position open.
    strategy.close("B1", comment=b1TimeStop ? "Time stop " + str.tostring(tsMin) + "m" : "EOD",
         alert_message='{"ticker":"SPX", "action":"exit"}')

if b2Up or b2Dn
    b2Dir := b2Up ? 1 : -1
if b3Up or b3Dn
    b3Dir := b3Up ? 1 : -1

// ==================== SPREAD SUGGESTIONS + VISUALS ====================
psS = math.floor(close * (1 - otmPct) / strikeStep) * strikeStep
csS = math.ceil(close * (1 + otmPct) / strikeStep) * strikeStep
f0(x) => str.tostring(x, "#")
if b2Up or b2Dn
    label.new(bar_index, b2Up ? low : high,
      "BOT2 SELL 5-wide " + (b2Up ? "PUT spread " + f0(psS) + "/" + f0(psS - 5) : "CALL spread " + f0(csS) + "/" + f0(csS + 5)) + " 0DTE\nclose @50% credit · stop @2x",
      style=b2Up ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color=color.new(color.blue, 20), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
if b3Up or b3Dn
    label.new(bar_index, b3Up ? low : high,
      "BOT3 SELL 10-wide " + (b3Up ? "PUT spread " + f0(psS) + "/" + f0(psS - 10) : "CALL spread " + f0(csS) + "/" + f0(csS + 10)) + " 0DTE\nclose @50% credit · stop @2x",
      style=b3Up ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, color=color.new(color.purple, 20), textcolor=color.white, size=size.small)
plot(isRTH and rthIx > 2  ? hi15 : na, "OR15 High", color.new(color.teal, 40),  2, plot.style_linebr)
plot(isRTH and rthIx > 2  ? lo15 : na, "OR15 Low",  color.new(color.teal, 40),  2, plot.style_linebr)
plot(isRTH and rthIx > 5  ? hi30 : na, "OR30 High", color.new(color.blue, 55),  1, plot.style_linebr)
plot(isRTH and rthIx > 5  ? lo30 : na, "OR30 Low",  color.new(color.blue, 55),  1, plot.style_linebr)
plot(isRTH and rthIx > 11 ? hi60 : na, "OR60 High", color.new(color.purple, 55),1, plot.style_linebr)
plot(isRTH and rthIx > 11 ? lo60 : na, "OR60 Low",  color.new(color.purple, 55),1, plot.style_linebr)

// ==================== SPREAD ALERTS ====================
alertcondition(b2Up, "BOT2 UP — sell PUT spread",  "SPX BOT2: 30m OR broke UP. SELL 5-wide PUT credit spread ~0.30% OTM. Close @50% credit, stop @2x.")
alertcondition(b2Dn, "BOT2 DN — sell CALL spread", "SPX BOT2: 30m OR broke DOWN. SELL 5-wide CALL credit spread ~0.30% OTM. Close @50% credit, stop @2x.")
alertcondition(b3Up, "BOT3 UP — sell PUT spread",  "SPX BOT3: 60m OR broke UP. SELL 10-wide PUT credit spread ~0.30% OTM. Close @50% credit, stop @2x.")
alertcondition(b3Dn, "BOT3 DN — sell CALL spread", "SPX BOT3: 60m OR broke DOWN. SELL 10-wide CALL credit spread ~0.30% OTM. Close @50% credit, stop @2x.")
